        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "c99dc0a0-7d67-5948-b404-c2eb2eeea902",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Tim McIlrath, Spike Slawson, Pete Wentz, Jay Jancetic, Daniel Binaei, Adam Bishop, Timothy Miller\n- Organizations: Arma Angelus, Rise Against, Me First and the Gimme Gimmes, Swingin' Utters, Filthy Thievin' Bastards, Re-Volts, Uke-Hunt, Fall Out Boy, Holy Roman Empire, Harm's Way, Racetraitor, Last Action Zeros, Mission Viejo High School, Immortal Art Tattoo & Body Piercing\n- Places: Mission Viejo, California, Scottsdale, Arizona\n- Roles: musician, vocalist, bassist, guitarist, drummer, English teacher, owner\n\nFacts:\n- Tim McIlrath was born on November 3, 1978.\n- Tim McIlrath is an American punk rock musician.\n- Spike Slawson is an American punk rock musician.\n- Spike Slawson is a member of Me First and the Gimme Gimmes, Swingin' Utters, Filthy Thievin' Bastards, Re-Volts, and Uke-Hunt.\n- Arma Angelus included Pete Wentz on vocals, Tim McIlrath on bass guitar, Jay Jancetic on guitar, Daniel Binaei on guitar, Adam Bishop on guitar, and Timothy Miller on drums.\n- Pete Wentz later became the bass guitarist and a backing vocalist in Fall Out Boy.\n- Tim McIlrath later became the lead singer of Rise Against.\n- Jay Jancetic later played guitar for Holy Roman Empire and Harm's Way in Chicago.\n- Daniel Binaei was formerly a member of Racetraitor.\n- Adam Bishop later became an English teacher at Mission Viejo High School in Mission Viejo, California.\n- Timothy Miller later played drums for the Arizona-based punk band Last Action Zeros.\n- Timothy Miller later became the owner of Immortal Art Tattoo & Body Piercing in Scottsdale, Arizona.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "deb4ceac-7305-5f52-813d-f90b254b96f8",
